20 0 obj
<< /A 308 0 R /Alt (MRI images of the pelvic region. Panel 1a, dated February 2024, shows an area highlighted by a red arrow. Panel 1b, from September 2025, and panel 1c, a few days later, also highlight regions with red arrows, indicating changes over time.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 15 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 309 0 R /Alt (Timeline of rectal tumor treatment from February 2024 to September 2025. Initial diagnosis: cT3N2, MRF-, EMVI+, wtRas, wtBraf, Her2 negative, MSI-H. Nivolumab 240 milligrams every two weeks, followed by non-operative management with digital rectal examination, endoscopy, and MRI every three months. Observations indicate near complete response by June 2024 and clinical complete responses from September 2024 onward.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 310 0 R /Alt (Graph on the left shows TSH and fT4 levels over time with TSH in blue and fT4 in orange. Thiamazole and levothyroxine treatments are indicated. Graph on the right shows creatinine levels over time with a peak at C8 after a CT scan.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
